<h1>Food security by state or province: USA, Canada, Brazil</h1>
<p>"Food insecure" means a household (or person) lacked reliable access to enough food because of money or other resources. "Food secure" is the remainder. Bars show the food-insecure share.</p>
<div class="box"><strong>Read before comparing.</strong> Each country uses a different survey, unit (households vs people), year and scale, so rates must not be compared across charts. I read "food safety" as food security (access to enough food); food safety in the sense of contamination is a different topic. Canada and Brazil charts show only the regions I could verify, as noted under each.</div>
